27
00:01:56,000 --> 00:01:59,917
Now, the restaurant side. The Green Table tracks ingredient batches, expiry

28
00:01:59,917 --> 00:02:03,833
dates and consumption history, with CSV imports for both inventory and

29
00:02:03,833 --> 00:02:07,750
usage. Amazon Chronos Two forecasts consumption. Inventory logic then accounts for

30
00:02:07,750 --> 00:02:11,667
expiring batches and funded incoming orders to suggest replenishment. The chart

31
00:02:11,667 --> 00:02:15,583
also compares a simple baseline. On this synthetic example, that baseline

32
00:02:15,583 --> 00:02:19,500
